I come home from my new job.
Outside the building, I meet Nina.
She is walking her little dog.
"Hello Maya," says Nina.
"How is the new job?" she asks.
"It is really good," I say.
"The office is nice, and my colleagues are kind."
We stand on the pavement and talk a little.
"I have tomorrow morning off," I say.
"I am going to the municipality."
"I need to get my CPR number."
Nina nods.
"Do you have a Danish phone number?" she asks.
"No, not yet," I answer.
"You need a Danish number for the forms," says Nina.
"Buy a SIM card first."
"Thanks for the tip," I say.
Nina and the dog walk on.
I go inside.
